# Credentials. The Atlassian token, the GitHub token and the Anthropic key all
# live in .env, and none of them belong in git.
.env

# Run history is per-machine demo state: whoever clones this will produce their
# own, and committing it would collide on every pull.
data/runs.sqlite
data/runs.sqlite-shm
data/runs.sqlite-wal

# Chroma's HNSW segment directory, named by collection uuid. Derived, not
# source: Chroma rebuilds it from chroma.sqlite3 on first query, and it is
# rewritten on every read, so committing it produces a permanently dirty tree
# and binary churn in unrelated commits. Verified regenerating from sqlite
# alone -- 43 chunks, identical scores.
data/*/

# Model weights, if setup puts them here. 3.6GB.
models/

# NOTE: docs/ and data/ ARE committed on purpose.
#   docs/  the Confluence corpus as Markdown — 83KB, and the thing that makes
#          the retrieval reviewable without an Atlassian account
#   data/  the Chroma index — chroma.sqlite3 and index-meta.json only, so the
#          demo runs without credentials. The uuid segment directory beside
#          them is derived and ignored.
# Both are reproducible with `ingest` + `index`; they are committed so that
# someone without access to the space can still run this.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
